## Pitch

Ledger Garden is a local-first record organizer for small volunteer groups and neighborhood associations. It keeps their lists useful without an account by importing, checking and storing records on their own machine.

## What makes this different

Unlike hosted spreadsheets, Ledger Garden works without a network account. Groups retain direct control of their records, accepting fewer collaboration features in return.


## Who it is for

Volunteer coordinators who maintain modest lists on one shared computer and need readable, exportable records.

## Who it is not for

Large organizations needing simultaneous remote editing, cloud administration or live analytics.

## What it commits to

Ordinary list work remains available offline. Invalid import input leaves existing records unchanged. Users can inspect and export every stored record.

## What it refuses to be

It does not become an advertising service, mandatory cloud account or remote surveillance tool.

## What would prove this wrong

The direction fails if ordinary list work needs network access, groups cannot recover readable exports, or import validation silently loses existing records.

","56c5223573a896984d202f85631242479d13d36742bab34ab20513bd7abfbf01":"# Strategic positioning

`VISION.md` is the canonical project-vision artifact. This supporting rationale explains how the vision was derived and does not independently override it.

## Project category

Local-first record organizer.

## Primary user

Small volunteer groups and neighborhood associations maintaining lists on a shared computer.

## Primary pain

Hosted tools require accounts and reliable connectivity for simple record work.

## Primary promise

Useful, readable records remain under the group’s local control.

## Core mechanism

Import, validate and store locally, with inspectable export.

## Alternatives

Hosted spreadsheets offer richer simultaneous collaboration. Plain text offers less structured validation.

## Tradeoff

Local control and offline operation take priority over remote collaboration.

## Compatibility surfaces

Python, JSON files and command-line invocation are implementation compatibility choices, not the product category.

## Refusals

No mandatory cloud account, advertising or remote surveillance.

## Falsifiability

Ordinary use requiring network access, unrecoverable exports or silent record loss contradicts the promise.
